# [WEB-CACHE-1 2026-08-26] Cache policy for avatok.ai.
#
# THE BUG THIS FIXES
#   Every HTML response was going out as
#     cache-control: public, max-age=2678400, must-revalidate
#   2678400 seconds is 31 days — Cloudflare's DEFAULT Browser Cache TTL, not
#   anything this repo asked for. Nothing set a header, so the zone default
#   applied to the pages themselves.
#
#   The effect: a visitor who had ever loaded avatok.ai kept that exact HTML for
#   a month. Deploys were invisible to them. Worse, the HTML holds hashed
#   /_astro/<name>.<hash>.css references, and those files are replaced on every
#   deploy — so a month-old page asks for a stylesheet that no longer exists and
#   renders as raw unstyled markup with whatever navigation it shipped with.
#   That is exactly the "site looks fucked" report on 2026-08-26: an old cached
#   homepage with the retired Receptionist nav and no CSS, while the live site
#   was fine for anyone loading it fresh.
#
#   `must-revalidate` does NOT save you here. It only governs what happens once
#   an entry is already STALE; for the 31 days the entry is fresh the browser
#   never asks the server anything.
#
# THE RULE
#   HTML is the index that names every hashed asset, so it must never outlive a
#   deploy. Everything content-hashed can be cached forever, because a new build
#   produces a new filename rather than new contents at the same URL.

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Content-hashed by Astro — the filename changes whenever the bytes do, so these
# are safe to pin for a year and are what keeps repeat visits fast.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Self-hosted woff2, versioned by deploy path and never edited in place.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
